num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Before concluding arbitrage has failed, the board should first rule out measurement artifacts:**\n\n- **Timing:** Does the NAV strike match the official closing auction? Check for stale or fair-valued prices, late corporate actions, and accrual and cash treatment.\n- **Peers:** Do similar ETFs and index futures show the same pattern? If so, the cause is likely market-wide (sector stress, factor dislocation).\n- **Underlying frictions:** Examine illiquid, small-cap or hard-to-borrow constituents, wide spreads, short-sale constraints, and settlement or basket mismatches.\n- **AP and market-maker participation:** Review active AP count, creation/redemption volumes, fee or cutoff changes, balance-sheet constraints, and lead market maker quoting quality.\n\n**Inquiry:** Request the adviser's documented analysis of intraday iNAV versus price, basket data and AP interviews.\n\n**Corrective options:** Adjust custom baskets or cash-in-lieu rules, revise transaction fees, recruit more APs or market makers, refine fair-value procedures, or enhance disclosure. Under Rule 6c-11, a premium or discount above 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days requires a website explanation, not automatic remediation.","ttft_ms":2034,"type":"result","duration_ms":4942,"uuid":"77a12188-329b-44cc-86d5-180574223c74","ttft_stream_ms":1381,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":1381,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
